# Passive open via --listen. Peer connects to us; we go through
# LISTEN → SYN_RCVD → ESTABLISHED. The peer port/IP are pinned by the
# first inbound SYN.

--listen 10.0.0.1:80 iss 0x55555555 peer_iss 0xAAAA0000

# Peer's SYN. Carries WS so we negotiate WS back.
+0 < SEW 0:0(0) win 32768 <mss 1460, wscale 7, sackOK, TS val 1 ecr 0>

# Our SYN-ACK echoes ECE (no CWR), WS, sackOK, TS. Per RFC 7323 §2.3
# SYN-ACK windows are NEVER scaled — they saturate at u16::MAX = 65535
# regardless of what BUF_CAP advertises post-handshake.
+0 > SE. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460, wscale 5, sackOK, TS val * ecr 1>

# Peer's third ACK.
+.005 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 32768 <TS val 2 ecr *>

--expect_state ESTABLISHED
